<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105728" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρῡσ-ίππιον</span></b> , τό,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρύω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a mark branded on the jaw of a horse
			superannuated</i> in the public service, <i><span class="en">
				Eup.
				318
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Zen.
				4.41
			</span></i>: the metre of <i><span class="en">
				Eup.
			</span></i> shows that <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρυσίππειον,</span> as
			written in <i><span class="en">
				Ael.Dion.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				311
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				7.186
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				771.16
			</span></i>, is incorrect.—The horse was <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρύσιππος</span></b> , ὁ, <i><span class="en">
				Theognost.
				<u>Can.</u>
				24
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
